From da2702c347218dc933ac4c326acb723bac2698f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 18:05:39 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_ui: /btw asks a side question, answered in a card
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Zeo next proposal §6.8 (ask 29), the `/btw` half. A composer message that
starts with `/btw` goes to the agent at once -- while a turn runs it is
not queued behind it, and Send Now does not stop the turn for it --
through Claude Agent (Plus) 0.38.0's `_claude/btw`, and the answer shows
in a dismissable card above the composer. The answer never enters the
conversation: the agent keeps it out of the session's transcript.

- acp_thread: AgentConnection gains supports_side_question and
  ask_side_question -> SideAnswer {answer, fallback_model}; the default
  refuses. SIDE_QUESTION_MAX_CHARS (8000) is plus's own limit
  (BTW_MAX_QUESTION_CHARS), checked before asking.
- agent_servers (v1): `_claude/btw` {sessionId, question} through
  send_task_request when the agent advertises `_claude/btw`.
  parse_side_question_answer reads `answered` (an answer without text is
  an error, never an empty card) and turns no_answer, unsupported and
  failed into words.
- agent_ui: send() and interrupt_and_send() hand the composer to
  send_side_question first; it takes the message only when the agent
  answers side questions and the text is `/btw` as the whole first word
  (side_question_invocation, as plus's parseBtwInvocation reads it), and
  clears the composer. A bare `/btw` shows how to use it; a question past
  the limit is refused in the card. The card (SideQuestionCard, per
  thread view) keeps to the composer's column (§6.30) below the context
  card: "By the way", the question, a dismiss button, the answer as
  Markdown in a 240 px body that scrolls with an always-visible bar, and
  "Not added to the conversation" (with the fallback model when one
  answered). A new question replaces the card and drops the earlier
  request's task, so a late answer never lands in a newer card.

An agent that does not advertise `_claude/btw` gets `/btw` as before, as
a prompt (plus answers that too, as an agent message). The composer's
history (0044) is read from the transcript, so Up does not recall a
side question.

Tests: v1::side_question_tests (4) -- an answer with and without its
fallback model, `answered` without text is an error, every other status
in words; side_question_card::tests (4) -- the question after the
command, a bare command asks for usage, anything else is not a side
question (`/btwx`, a prompt that mentions /btw), the limit counted in
characters. Seen failing: three probes at once, each on its own function
(the whole-word check removed, the limit counted in bytes, an answer
without text accepted) failed exactly those three tests. Xvfb proof with
a stub agent that holds its turn for 25 s, in the hub:
docs/assets/zeo-6.8-btw-and-steer-2026-11-15/ (the stub received one
prompt and one `_claude/btw` with the question; the card answered while
the turn ran, nothing was queued, and the transcript after the turn held
the prompt and its reply only).
---

